  "notes": "Vercel REST API is documented at vercel.com/docs/rest-api with 400+ endpoints across dozens of resource groups (projects, deployments, domains, dns, env vars, edge-config, webhooks, teams, etc). Auth is via personal Bearer access tokens created in Account Settings (free on the Hobby plan) or OAuth2 tokens issued to Marketplace/native integrations (response schema shows token type \\\"oauth2-token\\\" with origin e.g. \\\"github\\\"). No app review needed to create a personal token and call the API; building a distributable OAuth integration for the Marketplace goes through Vercel's integration developer flow but isn't required for basic API/agent use. Vercel publishes vercel/mcp-handler, an official SDK/framework for building MCP servers on Vercel (used by the community mcp-vercel server too), though it is a framework rather than a single hosted MCP endpoint.",
